>Well if it only happened on average once per game and maybe twice when
>unlucky it wouldn't seem to be to bad. I mean the odds of it occuring and
>the mysterious force happening would be low. Which means it would happen
>every game but still it probably wouldn't happen more then once.

That's almost impossible to achive.  If it's done randomly, you're
looking at a binomial distribution.  If you want 2 to be rare, 3 and
higher are even rarer.  This means that 0 and 2 are about equally
likely.  Given the number of levels this applies to, getting to
"usually" one just isn't possible.

An alternative would be for the game to randomly choose when this
happened once per game, but . . .

